{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to the prior comment (do not auto-close yet). The substantive fix HAS landed on main (commit 7501cc1d, this ticket's trailer) and 7 of 8 acceptance criteria verify green on the tree: AC1 pin present, AC2 no workflow diff, AC3 check_uv_pin.py exits 0, AC4 test_uv_pin_guard.py 11 passed, AC5 Makefile wires the guard, plus the two CI-log ACs are evidenced in the commit body (run 33230196661). BUT the close gate correctly blocks: AC8 ('upgrading uv is a one-line change', proxied by `grep -rlF '0.12.7' pyproject.toml Makefile scripts/check_uv_pin.py | wc -l -eq 1`) FAILS with count=2. The second match is NOT a second copy of the pin — it is illustrative docstring prose in scripts/check_uv_pin.py:16-17 (`==0.12.7` vs a range `>=0.12.7`, explaining why the exact form skips the network). The authoritative pin lives in exactly one place (pyproject.toml:354), so the AC's INTENT holds; only its literal-grep proxy trips on doc examples. Owner decision needed (not forcing): either (a) reword AC8 to target the authoritative pin only / tag it [non-codebase] with this evidence, or (b) make the docstring examples version-agnostic (e.g. `==<pin>` / `>=<pin>`) so the single-source grep passes. Leaving in_progress for that call. Residual artifact-URL fetch remains tracked separately by 5caa-4b63."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788223056332936001,"uuid":"5a0f4c71-a6c3-4a26-b350-32b9f044efd5"}